  <h2>Why agents centralise prepaid wallets</h2>
  <p>
    Cross-border marketplace APIs rarely expose stable overseas-card checkout surfaces; aggregators therefore prefund procurement ledgers reconciled against Taobao-class sellers.
    Treat Kakobuy balances as <strong>working capital for procurement</strong>, not interest-bearing deposits—returns and disputes discussed in <a href="/blog/kakobuy-domestic-returns-before-international-ship/">domestic returns playbook</a> still manipulate ledger states once funds settle.</p>

  <h2>Rail catalogue (always verify live menus)</h2>
  <h3>Card networks</h3>
  <p>
    Visa/Mastercard-class rails balance convenience against issuer neuroticism: China-facing MCC codes occasionally trigger declines even after slick 3DS animations succeed.</p>
  <p>
    Track whether charges post as immediate authorisations or multi-stage captures—authorization holds can collide with secondary purchase attempts during flash promotions sourced via <a href="/blog/kakobuy-coupons/">coupon realism</a>.</p>
  <h3>Alternative payment methods</h3>
  <p>
    Regional wallets and bank redirects appear/disappear as acquirers refresh compliance posture; Discord screenshots proving availability yesterday rarely survive next Tuesday.</p>
  <h3>Push-style bank transfers</h3>
  <p>
    Lower interchange sometimes trades for slower settlement—dangerous when <a href="/blog/kakobuy-warehouse-storage-spreadsheet/">warehouse storage clocks</a> approach forfeiture thresholds.</p>

  <h2>FX spreads &amp; multi-currency mental accounting</h2>
  <p>
    Shopping agents surface hybrid quoting: storefront yuan, dashboard USD/EUR presentation and card-statement currencies may all diverge.</p>
  <p>
    Tiny spreads compound across consolidated parcels rehearsed in <a href="/blog/kakobuy-rehearsal-packaging-freight/">freight estimates</a>; spreadsheet shoppers should screenshot dashboard FX panels whenever reconciling bank CSV exports—not because Kakobuy is uniquely opaque, but because issuing banks stack hidden markup atop acquirer spreads.</p>
  <p>
    Idle wallet balances expressed in one currency while procurement ticks in another can drift quietly during volatile macro weeks—model idle cash consciously during holiday stacks outlined in <a href="/blog/china-public-holidays-agent-forwarding-2026/">2026 holiday calendar essay</a>.</p>

  <h2>Coupons, rebates &amp; ledger traps</h2>
  <p>
    Promotions intersect balances messily—shipping vouchers may apply only after wallet thresholds clear while simultaneously blocking withdrawals.</p>
  <p>
    Apply scepticism modelled in coupon essay before assuming stackable savings; promotional credit sometimes imprisons funds toward future parcels with no cash-out lane.</p>

  <h2>Chargebacks, disputes &amp; ethical boundaries</h2>
  <p>
    Friendly fraud chargebacks after successful QC poison acquirer relationships for entire shopper cohorts—agents ban aggressively when patterns emerge.</p>
  <p>
    Legitimate fraud belongs at issuer fraud desks with police references when warranted; “batch disappointment” belongs in marketplace dispute portals—not issuer clawbacks.</p>

  <h2>Security checklist before large top-ups</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Hostname discipline:</strong> verify TLS certificates visually—phishing clones spike whenever spreadsheet seasons trend on TikTok.</li>
    <li><strong>Incremental funding:</strong> ramp balances slowly until QC cadence from <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">QC primer</a> stabilises.</li>
    <li><strong>Receipt discipline:</strong> export Kakobuy receipts immediately; banks dispute timelines exceed warehouse patience.</li>
    <li><strong>Descriptor literacy:</strong> note acquirer descriptors now so month-end statements reconcile without panic.</li>
    <li><strong>Secret hygiene:</strong> never paste PAN data into Discord bots—social engineering dwarfs technical hacking risk.</li>
  </ol>

